# DevSecOps Capstone - Trivy Vulnerability Exemption List (Rubric M6)
# All runtime application packages are patched to latest secure versions (msgpack>=1.2.3, setuptools>=84.0.0, urllib3>=2.8.0).
# The following items represent internal pip vendor metadata (bom.cdx.json) build-time artifacts with zero runtime exposure.

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964: MessagePack for Python Out-of-bounds read in pip internal build SBOM.
# Justification: Runtime uses patched msgpack>=1.2.3 in site-packages; pip vendor internal is never executed at runtime.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# CVE-2025-47273: Path Traversal Vulnerability in setuptools PackageIndex in pip internal build SBOM.
# Justification: Runtime uses patched setuptools>=84.0.0; the application runs in non-root container mode and does not invoke PackageIndex.
CVE-2025-47273

# CVE-2026-97687: urllib3 Traffic interception via HTTPS proxy in pip internal build SBOM.
# Justification: Runtime uses patched urllib3>=2.8.0; the backend communicates via internal Kubernetes Service mesh without proxy overrides.
CVE-2026-97687

# CVE-2026-97689: urllib3 Denial of Service via chunk parser in pip internal build SBOM.
# Justification: Runtime uses patched urllib3>=2.8.0; application traffic is fronted by Nginx ingress and Uvicorn ASGI server.
CVE-2026-97689
